IMPORT prelude

-- A New Tax System (Medicare Levy Surcharge--Fringe Benefits) Act 1999 (Commonwealth of Australia) -- do I pay the Medicare
-- levy surcharge on my reportable fringe benefits total: s 4 (private patient hospital cover), s 5 (dependant), s 6 (tier 2 and
-- tier 3 earner, with the Private Health Insurance Act 2007 s 22-30 tables as s 6(3) modifies them), s 7 (when people are
-- married: de facto and registered couples, living apart, a spouse who died), s 8 (prescribed person), s 10 (imposition on a
-- resident's reportable fringe benefits total), s 11 (the total of the Division amounts), s 12 (single, no dependants), s 13
-- (single, with dependants), ss 14-16 (married).
--
-- SEAT: the taxpayer without private patient hospital cover who receives reportable fringe benefits -- the employee whose
-- payment summary shows a reportable fringe benefits total, asking "Do I pay the surcharge on my fringe benefits, and how much?"
-- Every exported question is phrased as that person would ask it.
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 42, compilation date 1 July 2026, includes amendments up to Act No. 58, 2026 (Register id
-- C2026C00288), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A00412.txt. No instrument sets this Act's numbers: its one
-- figure, "$28,011" in ss 15(1)(c) and 16(2)(c), is in its own text. Also used: the Private Health Insurance Act 2007
-- ss 22-30, 22-35, 22-40 and 45-1, as deposited at
-- ../../../private-health-insurance-act-2007/registers/source-bundle/C2007A00031.txt (this Act borrows its tiers and thresholds
-- from there, and s 4 borrows its excess limits).
--
-- THE YEAR THE $28,011 IS FOR. The compilation states it once, with no year. It is the same figure as the Medicare Levy Act
-- 1986's s 8D(3)(c), and the same compilation date and amending Act (No. 58, 2026). INFERENCE, as in
-- ../../../medicare-levy-act-1986/encodings/baseline-2026-10: it is the figure for the 2025-26 year of income, and it stands for
-- later years until amended. For a married person (Division 4) in 2024-25 or earlier the amount is `Not in the deposited text`.
-- Divisions 2 and 3 use no figure of this Act's own, so their answers carry no year.
--
-- THE DEPOSIT DROPS EVERY FORMULA set as an image ("the amount worked out using the formula:" is followed by nothing): the
-- part-year formulas in ss 12(3), 13(4) and 16(4). So a part-year surcharge is `Not in the deposited text`, as in the Medicare
-- Levy Act baseline. The Private Health Insurance Act's tier thresholds are indexed under its s 22-45 and the indexed figures are
-- not deposited, so they are INPUTS; its s 22-40(4) increase for two or more dependent children is a formula the deposit also
-- drops, and is an INPUT.
--
-- A year of income is named by the calendar year in which it begins: 2025 is the 2025-26 year of income.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: ss 1, 2, 3(2), 9 (machinery and application); s 10(4) (application from 1999-2000: every year asked is later);
-- the s 10(1) note's offset for surcharge on lump sums in arrears (ITAA 1997 Subdiv 61-L); s 15(2)(b) and s 16(5)(b) (the
-- Schedule 2F s 271-105(1) assumption in working out a trust's net income: the spouse's trust share is asked as a figure);
-- rounding. Borrowed terms are asked as facts: "legally married" and "dependant" (Part VIIB of the 1936 Act, ss 251R, 251V, as
-- s 5 trims them), "prescribed person" (s 251U, as s 8 trims it), "income for surcharge purposes" (ITAA 1997), "reportable
-- fringe benefits total" (Fringe Benefits Tax Assessment Act 1986), "resident of Australia" (1936 Act s 6(1)), "complying health
-- insurance policy" and "hospital treatment" (PHI Act).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the individual to whom the law is applied, with
-- the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for
-- public use as advice. Consistent with ../../../medicare-levy-act-1986/encodings/baseline-2026-10, which imposes the surcharge
-- on taxable income; this Act imposes it on the reportable fringe benefits total. See NOTES.md.

§ `A New Tax System (Medicare Levy Surcharge--Fringe Benefits) Act 1999 -- the surcharge on fringe benefits`

§§ `Answers and helpers`

-- Every money answer is either an amount, or says plainly that the deposited compilation has no rule for the case.
DECLARE Answer IS ONE OF
    Amount HAS `value` IS A NUMBER
    `Not in the deposited text`

§§ `Which year the deposited figure is for`

-- See the header: INFERENCE that the $28,011 is the figure for 2025-26 and later.
@export Does the deposited text give the $28,011 figure for my year of income?
GIVEN `year` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year in which your year of income begins (2025 for 2025-26)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the deposited text give the figure for my year` IF `year` AT LEAST 2025

§§ `s 7 -- when people are married`

-- s 7(1): "This Act applies to 2 persons (whether of the same sex or different sexes) as if they were married to each other for a
-- period if: (a) their relationship is registered for the period under a law of a State or Territory prescribed for the purposes
-- of section 2E of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 ...; or (b) they lived together in a relationship as a couple on a genuine
-- domestic basis for the period, although not legally married to each other."
-- s 7(1A): "If, during the period, either or both of the persons was legally married to another person, or in a relationship
-- mentioned in paragraph (1)(a) with another person, this Act applies as if the person or persons were not legally married to,
-- or in a relationship mentioned in paragraph (1)(a) with, the other person."
-- s 7(2): "A person is taken not to be married to another person if they are living separately and apart."
-- (Gloss: "married" here takes in legal marriage, a registered relationship and a de facto couple. A de facto or registered
-- relationship with someone new displaces a legal marriage, or a registration, with someone else. Couples who live separately
-- and apart are not married. The Private Health Insurance Act 2007 s 22-30(1)(a) borrows this meaning for its families table.)
@export Am I married to this person for the Medicare levy surcharge on fringe benefits (s 7(1), (1A), (2))?
GIVEN `we are legally married` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and this person are legally married to each other
      `our relationship is registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your relationship is registered under a prescribed State or Territory relationships law
      `we live together as a couple on a genuine domestic basis` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you live together with this person as a couple on a genuine domestic basis
      `I or they are in a de facto or registered relationship with someone else` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, in the period, you or this person live as a couple with, or are registered with, a third person
      `we are living separately and apart` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and this person are living separately and apart
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I married to this person` IF
        (NOT `we are living separately and apart`)
    AND (   `we live together as a couple on a genuine domestic basis`
         OR (    (`we are legally married` OR `our relationship is registered`)
             AND (NOT `I or they are in a de facto or registered relationship with someone else`)))

-- s 7(3): "If: (a) the last person (the deceased) to whom another person was married during a year of income died during the
-- year of income; and (b) the death occurred while they were married; the living person is taken to be married to the deceased
-- during the period starting on the day the deceased died and ending on 30 June of the year of income."
@export Am I still taken to be married to my spouse who died, until 30 June (s 7(3))?
GIVEN `my spouse died during the year of income` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person you were married to died during this year of income
      `we were married when they died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were married to them (as s 7 reads it) when they died
      `they were the last person I was married to in the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether nobody else became your spouse later in the same year
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I taken to be married to my spouse who died` IF
        `my spouse died during the year of income`
    AND `we were married when they died`
    AND `they were the last person I was married to in the year`

§§ `s 4 -- private patient hospital cover`

-- s 4: "a person is covered by an insurance policy that provides private patient hospital cover if: (a) the policy is a
-- complying health insurance policy (within the meaning of the Private Health Insurance Act 2007) that covers hospital treatment
-- ...; and (b) any excess payable in respect of benefits under the policy is no more than the applicable amount set out in
-- section 45-1 of that Act in any 12 month period." PHI Act s 45-1: "(a) $750 in any 12 month period, in relation to a policy
-- under which only one person is insured; and (b) $1,500 in any 12 month period, in relation to any other policy."
-- (Same rule, same figures, as the Medicare Levy Act s 3(5).)
@export Does my health insurance policy count as private patient hospital cover for the surcharge on fringe benefits (s 4)?
GIVEN `a complying health insurance policy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the policy is a complying health insurance policy under the Private Health Insurance Act 2007
      `covers hospital treatment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the policy covers hospital treatment
      `only one person insured` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether only one person is insured under the policy
      `excess payable in any 12 months` IS A NUMBER @desc The most excess payable under the policy in any 12-month period, in dollars
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my policy count as hospital cover` IF
        `a complying health insurance policy`
    AND `covers hospital treatment`
    AND `excess payable in any 12 months` AT MOST (IF `only one person insured` THEN 750 ELSE 1500)

§§ `ss 13(1)(b)(iii), 13(2), 14(1)(b), 14(2) -- the cover test on a day, for a person with a spouse or dependants`

-- s 13(1)(b)(iii) and s 14(1)(b): "the person, or at least one of the person's dependants, is not covered by an insurance policy
-- that provides private patient hospital cover". ss 13(2), 14(2): "(a) the person is taken to be covered ... if, apart from
-- subsection 251U(2) of the Assessment Act, the person would be a prescribed person for the period because of paragraph
-- 251U(1)(a), (b), (ca), (caa) or (cb) of that Act; and (b) disregard each of the person's dependants who: (i) is a prescribed
-- person for the period; or (ii) would be a prescribed person for the period apart from subsection 251U(2)". (Gloss: the s 251U
-- paragraphs are defence personnel and their families with free treatment, veterans and others with free treatment under the
-- named Acts, and people on certain social security or veterans' payments; whether I or a dependant would be one is asked as a
-- fact.) For s 12 (single, no dependants) only my own cover counts, and these special rules do not apply.
@export On this day, do I count as without hospital cover for myself or my family (ss 13(1)(b)(iii), 13(2), 14(1)(b), 14(2))?
GIVEN `I have private patient hospital cover` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are covered on this day by a policy that counts under s 4
      `I would be prescribed under s 251U(1)(a), (b), (ca), (caa) or (cb) but for s 251U(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you would be a prescribed person (defence, veterans or certain payments) but for your dependants
      `a dependant of mine without cover who is not, and would not be, a prescribed person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether at least one of your dependants is uncovered on this day and is not (and would not be apart from s 251U(2)) a prescribed person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I count as uncovered on this day` IF
       (    (NOT `I have private patient hospital cover`)
        AND (NOT `I would be prescribed under s 251U(1)(a), (b), (ca), (caa) or (cb) but for s 251U(2)`))
    OR `a dependant of mine without cover who is not, and would not be, a prescribed person`

§§ `The facts one taxpayer states for one year of income`

-- Which Division applies depends on whether, "during the whole of the period", the person is married and has dependants. The
-- person states the pattern across the year, after s 7 (worked out by the two s 7 questions above). "Dependant" is s 5: a
-- dependant for Part VIIB of the 1936 Act, "disregarding subsections 251R(4), (5), (6B), (6C) and (6D)" -- asked as a fact.
-- `dependants in the year` counts dependants other than a spouse.
DECLARE `Marriage in the year` IS ONE OF
    `married all year`
    `not married at any time in the year`
    `married for part of the year`

DECLARE `Dependants in the year` IS ONE OF
    `dependants all year`
    `no dependants at any time in the year`
    `dependants for part of the year`

DECLARE Taxpayer HAS
    `year of income begins` IS A NUMBER
    `resident of Australia at any time in the year` IS A BOOLEAN
    `reportable fringe benefits total` IS A NUMBER
    `income for surcharge purposes` IS A NUMBER
    `marriage in the year` IS A `Marriage in the year`
    `married on 30 June, if married for part of the year` IS A BOOLEAN
    `spouse's income for surcharge purposes` IS A NUMBER
    `spouse's share of trust net income assessed to the trustee under s 98` IS A NUMBER
    `dependants in the year` IS A `Dependants in the year`
    `days in the year of income` IS A NUMBER
    `days I was a prescribed person` IS A NUMBER
    `days I count as uncovered` IS A NUMBER
    `my singles tier 1 threshold` IS A NUMBER
    `my singles tier 2 threshold` IS A NUMBER
    `my singles tier 3 threshold` IS A NUMBER
    `increase in my family thresholds for two or more children` IS A NUMBER

§§ `s 6 -- tier 2 and tier 3 earners`

-- s 6(1): "tier 2 earner" and "tier 3 earner" have their Private Health Insurance Act 2007 meanings "for the financial year
-- corresponding to the year of income". s 6(2), (3) replace PHI Act s 22-30(1)(b) by: "(b) on any day in the year, the person
-- has one or more dependants (within the meaning of the A New Tax System (Medicare Levy Surcharge--Fringe Benefits) Act 1999),
-- other than a dependant to whom the person is married (within the meaning of that Act)".
-- PHI Act s 22-30(1): the families table applies if "(a) on the last day of the financial year, the person is married (within
-- the meaning of the A New Tax System (Medicare Levy Surcharge--Fringe Benefits) Act 1999)" or (b), as replaced; s 22-30(2): the
-- spouse's "income for surcharge purposes ... [is] included in the first person's"; s 22-30(4): otherwise the singles table.
-- Each table: tier 1 above the tier 1 threshold up to tier 2; tier 2 above tier 2 up to tier 3; tier 3 above tier 3.
-- s 22-35: singles thresholds $90,000 / $105,000 / $140,000 "for the 2021-22 and 2022-23 financial year", indexed under s 22-45
-- -- the indexed figures are not deposited, so they are INPUTS. s 22-40(1)-(3): each family threshold is "double" the singles
-- one; s 22-40(4): increased for 2 or more dependent children "by the result of the following formula" (not in the deposit --
-- an INPUT). s 3(1): "family tier 1 threshold" and "singles tier 1 threshold" carry the PHI Act meanings.
DECLARE Tier IS ONE OF
    `not above the tier 1 threshold`
    `a tier 1 earner`
    `a tier 2 earner`
    `a tier 3 earner`

GIVEN `p` IS A Taxpayer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`p is married on 30 June` MEANS
    CONSIDER `p`'s `marriage in the year`
    WHEN `married all year` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `not married at any time in the year` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `married for part of the year` THEN `p`'s `married on 30 June, if married for part of the year`

GIVEN `p` IS A Taxpayer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the families table applies to p` MEANS
    `p is married on 30 June` `p`
    OR (CONSIDER `p`'s `dependants in the year`
        WHEN `no dependants at any time in the year` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE)

GIVEN `p` IS A Taxpayer, `singles` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`p's threshold from` MEANS
    IF `the families table applies to p` `p`
    THEN 2 TIMES `singles` PLUS `p`'s `increase in my family thresholds for two or more children`
    ELSE `singles`

GIVEN `p` IS A Taxpayer
GIVETH A NUMBER
`p's income for the tiers` MEANS
    IF `p is married on 30 June` `p`
    THEN `p`'s `income for surcharge purposes` PLUS `p`'s `spouse's income for surcharge purposes`
    ELSE `p`'s `income for surcharge purposes`

@export Which private health insurance income tier am I in, for the surcharge on fringe benefits (s 6; PHI Act s 22-30)?
GIVEN `p` IS A Taxpayer @desc Your facts for the year of income
GIVETH A Tier
DECIDE `Which income tier am I in` IS
    IF `p's income for the tiers` `p` GREATER THAN `p's threshold from` `p` (`p`'s `my singles tier 3 threshold`) THEN `a tier 3 earner`
    ELSE IF `p's income for the tiers` `p` GREATER THAN `p's threshold from` `p` (`p`'s `my singles tier 2 threshold`) THEN `a tier 2 earner`
         ELSE IF `p's income for the tiers` `p` GREATER THAN `p's threshold from` `p` (`p`'s `my singles tier 1 threshold`) THEN `a tier 1 earner`
              ELSE `not above the tier 1 threshold`

§§ `ss 11-14 -- which Division applies, and for how long`

-- s 11: "The amount of surcharge payable ... is the total of the amounts worked out under whichever of Divisions 2, 3 and 4 apply
-- to the person for a period in the year of income."
-- s 12(1)(b): during the whole of the period "(i) the person is not a married person; and (ii) the person does not have any
-- dependants; and (iii) the person is not covered ...; and (iv) the person is not a prescribed person."
-- s 13(1)(b): "(i) the person is not a married person; and (ii) the person has one or more dependants; and (iii) the person, or
-- at least one of the person's dependants, is not covered ...; and (iv) the person is not a prescribed person."
-- s 14(1): "(a) the person is a married person; and (b) the person, or at least one of the person's dependants, is not covered
-- ...; and (c) the person is not a prescribed person."
-- One case is one year; a change of marriage or dependants inside the year puts different Divisions on different days, and the
-- part-year formulas for that are not in the deposit.
DECLARE `Surcharge Division` IS ONE OF
    `Division 2 -- single, no dependants`
    `Division 3 -- single, with dependants`
    `Division 4 -- married`
    `more than one Division in the year`

DECLARE `Surcharge period` IS ONE OF
    `the whole year`
    `part of the year`
    `none of the year`

@export Which Division of the surcharge on fringe benefits would apply to me (ss 12, 13, 14)?
GIVEN `p` IS A Taxpayer @desc Your facts for the year of income
GIVETH A `Surcharge Division`
DECIDE `Which Division applies to me` IS
    CONSIDER `p`'s `marriage in the year`
    WHEN `married all year` THEN `Division 4 -- married`
    WHEN `married for part of the year` THEN `more than one Division in the year`
    WHEN `not married at any time in the year` THEN
        CONSIDER `p`'s `dependants in the year`
        WHEN `dependants all year` THEN `Division 3 -- single, with dependants`
        WHEN `no dependants at any time in the year` THEN `Division 2 -- single, no dependants`
        WHEN `dependants for part of the year` THEN `more than one Division in the year`

-- The period: every day on which I count as uncovered (s 12: I have no cover; ss 13, 14: the day test above) and I am not a
-- prescribed person (s 8: a prescribed person for Part VIIB of the 1936 Act, "disregarding subsection 251U(3)" -- asked as a
-- number of days). Where days of both kinds fall in the year, how they overlap is not asked, and the answer is `part of the year`.
@export For how much of the year am I uncovered and not a prescribed person, for the surcharge on fringe benefits (ss 12(1), 13(1), 14(1))?
GIVEN `p` IS A Taxpayer @desc Your facts for the year of income
GIVETH A `Surcharge period`
DECIDE `For how much of the year does the Division apply` IS
    IF     `p`'s `days I count as uncovered` AT MOST 0
        OR `p`'s `days I was a prescribed person` AT LEAST `p`'s `days in the year of income`
    THEN `none of the year`
    ELSE IF     `p`'s `days I count as uncovered` AT LEAST `p`'s `days in the year of income`
            AND `p`'s `days I was a prescribed person` AT MOST 0
         THEN `the whole year`
         ELSE `part of the year`

§§ `ss 12(1)(a), 13(1)(a), 15(1)(b)-(c), 15(2), 16(2), 16(3) -- the income test`

-- s 12(1)(a): "the person's income for surcharge purposes for the year of income exceeds the person's singles tier 1 threshold".
-- s 13(1)(a): "the person's income for surcharge purposes for the year of income exceeds the person's family tier 1 threshold".
-- s 15(1): "(b) the sum of the person's income for surcharge purposes, and the person's spouse's income for surcharge purposes,
-- for the year of income exceeds the person's family tier 1 threshold ...; and (c) the person's income for surcharge purposes for
-- the year of income exceeds $28,011." s 16(2) repeats (b) and (c) for a person "married for the whole of the year of income" to
-- whom Division 4 applies for part of the year. s 15(2), 16(5): if the spouse is "a beneficiary presently entitled to a share in
-- the net income of a trust estate in respect of which the trustee is liable to be assessed under section 98", "assume that: (a)
-- the spouse's income for surcharge purposes included that share". s 16(3): a person "married for only part of the year of
-- income" meets the test if "the person's income for surcharge purposes ... exceeds the person's family tier 1 threshold".
GIVEN `p` IS A Taxpayer
GIVETH A NUMBER
`p's family tier 1 threshold` MEANS
    2 TIMES `p`'s `my singles tier 1 threshold` PLUS `p`'s `increase in my family thresholds for two or more children`

GIVEN `p` IS A Taxpayer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`p meets the married-couple test` MEANS
        `p`'s `income for surcharge purposes` PLUS `p`'s `spouse's income for surcharge purposes`
            PLUS `p`'s `spouse's share of trust net income assessed to the trustee under s 98`
            GREATER THAN `p's family tier 1 threshold` `p`
    AND `p`'s `income for surcharge purposes` GREATER THAN 28011

-- For `more than one Division in the year`: the test of whichever Division could apply on some day. Married for part of the
-- year: s 16(3) for the married days, and s 12(1)(a) or s 13(1)(a) for the rest. Single with dependants for part of the year:
-- s 12(1)(a) or s 13(1)(a). Which uncovered days fall in which Division is not asked, so this answers whether the income test of
-- SOME Division that applies for some of the year is met.
GIVEN `p` IS A Taxpayer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`p meets the test of some Division` MEANS
    CONSIDER `p`'s `dependants in the year`
    WHEN `dependants all year` THEN `p`'s `income for surcharge purposes` GREATER THAN `p's family tier 1 threshold` `p`
    OTHERWISE `p`'s `income for surcharge purposes` GREATER THAN `p`'s `my singles tier 1 threshold`
           OR `p`'s `income for surcharge purposes` GREATER THAN `p's family tier 1 threshold` `p`

@export Is my income above the line at which the surcharge on fringe benefits starts (ss 12(1)(a), 13(1)(a), 15(1), 16(2), 16(3))?
GIVEN `p` IS A Taxpayer @desc Your facts for the year of income
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my income above the surcharge line` IF
    CONSIDER `Which Division applies to me` `p`
    WHEN `Division 2 -- single, no dependants` THEN
        `p`'s `income for surcharge purposes` GREATER THAN `p`'s `my singles tier 1 threshold`
    WHEN `Division 3 -- single, with dependants` THEN
        `p`'s `income for surcharge purposes` GREATER THAN `p's family tier 1 threshold` `p`
    WHEN `Division 4 -- married` THEN `p meets the married-couple test` `p`
    WHEN `more than one Division in the year` THEN `p meets the test of some Division` `p`

§§ `s 10 -- imposition, and must I pay`

-- s 10(1): "Medicare levy surcharge is imposed on the reportable fringe benefits total for a year of income of a person who is a
-- resident of Australia at any time during the year of income." s 10(2): resident "as defined in subsection 6(1) of the
-- Assessment Act" -- asked as a fact. (Gloss: the reportable fringe benefits total is the grossed-up value of fringe benefits
-- shown on my payment summary, a Fringe Benefits Tax Assessment Act 1986 term, asked as a figure.)
@export Must I pay the Medicare levy surcharge on my reportable fringe benefits for the year (ss 10-16)?
GIVEN `p` IS A Taxpayer @desc Your facts for the year of income
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I pay the surcharge on my fringe benefits` IF
        `p`'s `resident of Australia at any time in the year`
    AND `p`'s `reportable fringe benefits total` GREATER THAN 0
    AND (CONSIDER `For how much of the year does the Division apply` `p`
         WHEN `none of the year` THEN FALSE
         OTHERWISE TRUE)
    AND `Is my income above the surcharge line` `p`

§§ `The surcharge rate and amount`

-- ss 12(2), 13(3), 15(1): "1% of that total". ss 12(4), 13(5), 15(3), 16(4A): "Increase the amount of each percentage ... by 0.25
-- of a percentage point if the person is a tier 2 earner"; ss 12(5), 13(6), 15(4), 16(4B): "by 0.5 of a percentage point if the
-- person is a tier 3 earner". (Gloss: 1%, 1.25% or 1.5% of the REPORTABLE FRINGE BENEFITS TOTAL, though the test is on income for
-- surcharge purposes. Someone who meets the s 15 couple test only because of a spouse's trust share may be no tier earner at
-- all on the PHI Act tables; they pay the base 1%.)
@export At what rate is my surcharge on fringe benefits, in percent of my reportable fringe benefits total (ss 12, 13, 15, 16)?
GIVEN `p` IS A Taxpayer @desc Your facts for the year of income
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my surcharge rate` IS
    CONSIDER `Which income tier am I in` `p`
    WHEN `a tier 3 earner` THEN 1.5
    WHEN `a tier 2 earner` THEN 1.25
    OTHERWISE 1

GIVEN `p` IS A Taxpayer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`p's answer turns on the $28,011` MEANS
    CONSIDER `p`'s `marriage in the year`
    WHEN `married all year` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- The part-year formulas in ss 12(3), 13(4), 16(4) are not in the deposit: such a case is `Not in the deposited text`. So is a
-- married person's year before 2025-26 (the $28,011 in ss 15(1)(c) and 16(2)(c) is that year's figure).
@export How much Medicare levy surcharge do I pay on my reportable fringe benefits total (ss 10-16)?
GIVEN `p` IS A Taxpayer @desc Your facts for the year of income
GIVETH AN Answer
DECIDE `How much surcharge do I pay on my fringe benefits` IS
    IF (NOT `p`'s `resident of Australia at any time in the year`) THEN Amount 0
    ELSE IF `p's answer turns on the $28,011` `p`
            AND (NOT `Does the deposited text give the figure for my year` (`p`'s `year of income begins`))
         THEN `Not in the deposited text`
         ELSE IF (NOT `Must I pay the surcharge on my fringe benefits` `p`) THEN Amount 0
              ELSE CONSIDER `For how much of the year does the Division apply` `p`
                   WHEN `the whole year` THEN
                       CONSIDER `Which Division applies to me` `p`
                       WHEN `more than one Division in the year` THEN `Not in the deposited text`
                       OTHERWISE Amount (`p`'s `reportable fringe benefits total` TIMES `What is my surcharge rate` `p` DIVIDED BY 100)
                   OTHERWISE `Not in the deposited text`

§§ `The common case`

-- Asked with seven facts: resident, no spouse or dependants all year, never a prescribed person, hospital cover held (or not) all
-- year.
@export How much surcharge do I pay on my fringe benefits, if I am single with no dependants all year?
GIVEN `reportable fringe benefits total` IS A NUMBER @desc The reportable fringe benefits total on your payment summary, in dollars
      `income for surcharge purposes` IS A NUMBER @desc Your income for surcharge purposes for the year, in dollars
      `had private patient hospital cover all year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you held private patient hospital cover for the whole year
      `my singles tier 1 threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc Your singles tier 1 threshold for the year (Private Health Insurance Act s 22-35, as indexed), in dollars
      `my singles tier 2 threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc Your singles tier 2 threshold for the year, in dollars
      `my singles tier 3 threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc Your singles tier 3 threshold for the year, in dollars
GIVETH AN Answer
DECIDE `How much surcharge on my fringe benefits, simply` IS
    `How much surcharge do I pay on my fringe benefits`
        (Taxpayer 2025 TRUE `reportable fringe benefits total` `income for surcharge purposes`
                  `not married at any time in the year` FALSE 0 0 `no dependants at any time in the year`
                  365 0 (IF `had private patient hospital cover all year` THEN 0 ELSE 365)
                  `my singles tier 1 threshold` `my singles tier 2 threshold` `my singles tier 3 threshold` 0)
